  "verdict": "The relativistic periodic term is present with the IS-GPS-200 sign: a = 0.91 +/- 0.05 (formal, 5 windows, chi2 3.3/4) and a = 0.89 +/- 0.23 with leave-one-satellite-out (systematic-inclusive) errors. a = 0 is excluded at 17 sigma (formal) / 3.8 sigma (jackknife); a = 1 is consistent (1.7 / 0.5 sigma). With a free per-satellite quadratic nuisance a = 1.15 +/- 0.29. The phase-shifted null regressor (cos Ek, same amplitude) fits -0.20 +/- 0.12, which bounds residual once-per-rev systematics (single-frequency ionosphere, broadcast orbit/clock) at the ~15-20% level; per-satellite values scatter by ~+/-1 for the same reason, so the result is decisive for existence and sign, and ~20% in amplitude."
 },
 "data": {
  "carrier_source": "observations/telemetry_log.jsonl rows with per-sat carrier_cycles (10 s collector cadence, 2026-08-25 01:24 .. 2026-09-04 10:05 UTC; 403285 GPS samples); only rows after 2026-08-30 20:00 UTC used (commit 3107967 made the per-sat epoch the sample-accurate stream epoch; earlier epochs are wall-clock-at-emission and carry >1 m tag jitter)",
  "ephemeris": "BKG BRDC00WRD_R daily RINEX 3 (DOY 237-246, downloaded to scratchpad/brdc) + observations/brdc_latest.rnx (DOY 246-247); per-sample nearest-toe GPS record, |t-toe| <= 2.5 h, record switches flagged so no jump enters an increment; Klobuchar GPSA/GPSB from the daily headers (DOY 237-243; nearest day otherwise)",
