 "sign_derivation": "L = -(cycles_H - cycles_R) * c/f_L1 [m]. carrier_cycles rate == doppler_hz (archive check: ratio 0.9996, corr 0.9992); tracker Doppler is positive for closing range, so -lambda*cycles tracks +range: L = (rho_H-rho_R) - c(dt_sv_H-dt_sv_R) + tropo - iono + const. Empirical check per arc: doppler_sign_slope = slope of d(L)/dt against d(M)/dt, expected +1. M uses the broadcast polynomial clock only; Rreg = -c(dt_r_H - dt_r_R) with dt_r = F e sqrtA sin(Ek); a = +1 <=> IS-GPS-200 sign. Multi-satellite form: D_s = -cycles_s*lambda - [rho_s(t_tag+delta0) - c*poly_s + ZTD/sin(el) - I_klob]; regressor R_s = -c*dt_r,s so that a = +1 reproduces IS-GPS-200 (satellite clock reads early by dt_r>0 => carrier arrives with phase corresponding to a SHORTER apparent range, i.e. D decreases by c*dt_r).",
 "data_quality_findings": [
  "carrier_cycles is a true integrated phase: after removing common-mode terms the increment noise core is 1.8-2.1 cm per 10 s (0.1 cycle), but 25-35 %% of 10 s increments carry steps of 0.1-100 m.",
  "Steps are per-channel and mostly common-mode-proportional to range-rate: live.rs note_gap advances stream time through USB drop holes but does not propagate the NCO phase, so each hole of g seconds leaves a step ~ rdot_s*g (+ Costas half-cycle re-pull); such steps are absorbed exactly by the per-epoch (clock, g_k) projection, the rest are excluded as increment outliers.",
  "The stream epoch lags true receive time by a session-dependent constant: 4.4 s (Aug 31 - Sep 2 sessions), 45.2 s (Sep 1 19:04 - Sep 2 session), 2692 s (Sep 3 19:45 session); solved per window (delta0) and the model is re-evaluated at t_tag+delta0.",
  "Per-satellite ionospheric slant delay (single-frequency L1) varies by 5-15 m over a pass, the same order as the relativistic swing (10-22 m for e>=0.015 satellites); it is the dominant systematic and the reason per-satellite a values scatter by ~+/-1. A per-satellite VTEC x mapping nuisance is nearly collinear with sin(Ek) over a pass and destroys the conditioning (reported as iono_mapping_nuisance variants, not used).",
  "A per-channel code-epoch sawtooth (residual increment ~ rdot^2/c) was tested and is NOT present (binned medians within +/-3 mm vs 9-23 mm predicted)."
 ],
 "method": "Multi-satellite carrier-phase measurement of the GPS relativistic periodic\nclock term (per-epoch common-mode elimination; increment domain).\n\nPer window (a merged span of high-e slip-free arcs), all GPS satellites with\nslip-free carrier segments enter.  For sat s at tagged epoch t:\n    D_s = L_s - M_s,  L_s = -cycles_s * lambda,\n    M_s = rho_s(t_tag + delta0) - c*poly_s + ZTD/sin(el_s)\nFirst differences between consecutive samples (8-12 s) of one segment:\n    dD_s,k = dClock_k + rdot_s * g_k + a * dR_s,k + slope_seg * dt\n             (+ ddelta0 * d(rdot_s))  + eps\ndClock_k (receiver clock, common) and g_k (common time-tag / USB-hole\nincrement, proportional to each sat's range-rate) are free per epoch pair\nand eliminated exactly by per-epoch projection (Frisch-Waugh-Lovell),\nwhich needs >= 3 satellites per epoch.  Common-mode hole steps of ANY size\nare thereby removed; per-channel cycle slips remain and are handled by\nexcluding epoch pairs whose max |residual| exceeds THR.  delta0 (tagged\ntime -> true receive time) is solved and the model re-evaluated at\nt_tag + delta0 (2 passes) so second-order range terms are exact.\na = +1 <=> IS-GPS-200 relativistic term with its published sign\n(regressor R_s = -c * F e sqrtA sin Ek).\n",
